OVERVIEW:

 This program is a double-linked implementation of an indexed
 unsorted list. Instead of a normal indexed array, it uses nodes
 that track their predecessors and successors, with each node
 containing its respective element.


INCLUDED FILES:

 * ListTester.java - test class with full implementation of scenarios
 * IUDoubleLinkedList.java - double-linked node implementation of an
    indexed unsorted list
 * IndexedUnsortedList.java - interface class which IUDoubleLinkedList
    implements
 * Node.java - allows creation of nodes and links
 * README - documentation


COMPILING AND RUNNING:

 The driver class for testing is already configured to test
 the DoubleLinkedList implementation. The program first has
 to be compiled:
 $ javac ListTester.java

 The program is run with the command:
 $ java ListTester

 There are a few arguments when running the program that will
 change the output and/or formatting of the tests:
 * -a | to only print the failed tests
 * -s | to prevent printing the output of toString() calls
 * -m | to prevent printing section summaries

 To clean up the class files from compiling, run the command:
 $ rm *.class


